{
  "format": "helianthus-register-derived-names/v1",
  "description": "Register-derived value fields published by the gateway system, circuit and boiler planes, each with the published name, the native identity and the docs-ebus name of that register. service names the register family: B524 rows carry the opcode, group and register and the docs-ebus name and previous_name copied from the docs-ebus fixture protocols/vaillant/fixtures/b524-op02-register-names.csv (B524 opcode 0x02 register name catalog); B509 rows carry the operation opcode and the selector (fallback_selector, where present, is the second selector the gateway reads for the same value) and the docs-ebus name and legacy_api_path copied from the docs-ebus fixture protocols/vaillant/fixtures/b509-register-name-correspondence.csv (B509 register name correspondence). previous_name and legacy_api_path are documentary columns only: no surface publishes them. surfaces names the object that publishes the field on each surface (GraphQL type, MCP Go struct, Portal Go struct); an empty value means the surface does not publish the field. previous_published_name, where present, is the spelling the gateway published for the register before it adopted the docs-ebus name; no surface publishes it either. unit, where present, is the unit the GraphQL description of the field states instead of a name suffix; provisional marks a B509 register whose docs-ebus row carries an open question, and the GraphQL description of the field says the name is provisional. join, where present, records the second register of a field the gateway publishes as the join of two registers: the docs-ebus names of the two registers are the published name with the suffixes _prefix and _suffix. bound, where present, records the field that publishes the active write bound of the value: its published name is the value name with the suffix _bound, with its own previous published name and surfaces. exemption marks the single row whose published name is not yet the docs-ebus name, with the docs-ebus issue that settles it. unmapped_fields lists the fields of the recorded objects that no single register feeds; they keep their published name, with the reason. field_registers records every field of the GraphQL objects zone_state, zone_config, circuit_state, circuit_config, dhw_state and dhw_config: object names the GraphQL object; a field read from one B524 register carries its opcode, group and register and the docs-ebus name of that register; any other field carries derived, the B524 registers it combines (each written opcode/group/register; opcode 0x06 is a radio device register) and one sentence why it has no single register name, and a derived field without registers is one no B524 register feeds. A value the eeBUS overlay sets only while the register value is absent does not change the register of a field. pending lists every single-register field of field_registers whose published name still differs from the docs-ebus name of its register, with both names; it holds exactly that difference.",
  "source": "helianthus-docs-ebus protocols/vaillant/fixtures/b524-op02-register-names.csv; helianthus-docs-ebus protocols/vaillant/fixtures/b509-register-name-correspondence.csv",
